   "measured": "f0 117.9 Hz · centroid 1484 · presence 2-5 kHz 23.7% — the deepest voice in the set, and no longer the darkest: presence was 12.4% before the retune",
   "note": "A LEADER IS ONE VOICE, and it is a SHAPED one. It was the reference with an espeak overtone mixed on, and however that overtone was placed it was a second person — in the intelligibility band it formed words, and outside it it became a drone, which is worse. Two voices saying the same thing is unison, and unison is OVERLORD's idea. So: the reference at pitch 0.88 and speed 0.92 (about 88 Hz against neural's 101, a shade under a tenth slower), with a broadcast EQ instead of a companion, and the 0.85 s pause after every conclusion that makes it deliberate rather than merely slow. It inherits neural's clarity because it IS neural."
  },
  "declaredRate": "piper renders at 22050 Hz and the file is declared at 22050×0.88 = 19404 Hz for the 0.88 pitch; the measurement clip was resampled to 22050"
 },
 "note": "LEADER is ONE voice, shaped: the reference at speed 0.92 and pitch 0.88 under a four-band broadcast EQ, with a 0.85 s pause after every conclusion. No second speaker. Measured 83.5 Hz median here (75.8–95.5), the deepest voice in the set."
